    "SeasonRecapParagraphs": [
      "St. Andrew's built one of the strongest volleyball seasons in program history in 2003-04, finishing 19-3 under first-year head coach Mandy Stinson. The Saints moved quickly from an early 3-1 record into control of SCISA Region 2-AA, then kept stacking wins through September and October behind a senior-heavy roster and a young core that included freshman Mary Wilkowski.",
      "The region run became the backbone of the season. After beating Holly Hill on Sept. 23, St. Andrew's swept Beaufort, beat Colleton Prep, shut out James Island Christian, and posted back-to-back wins over Charleston Collegiate. A second victory over Holly Hill on Oct. 21 completed a 10-0 region mark, gave the Saints the SCISA 2-AA title, and secured the top south seed for the state tournament.",
      "St. Andrew's carried that form into the postseason. The Saints beat Greenwood Christian in the state tournament opener, then defeated Calhoun Academy twice on Oct. 25 to earn a place in the SCISA Class AA championship match. Becca Cooper, Carie Bugos, Mary Wilkowski, LeighAnne Evans, Grace Wilkowski, Becca Timms, Danielle Praino, Jennifer Lee, Maggie Hinchey, and Layne Haggberg all appeared in the recovered state-tournament stat lines.",
      "The season ended at Porter-Gaud School in Charleston, where undefeated Pee Dee Academy won the Class AA final 25-19, 25-13, 28-26. Even in defeat, the Saints pushed the final set deep and closed the year as SCISA AA State Runner-up after winning the region championship and reaching the state final for the first time after a semifinal finish the year before."
    ]
